1kpg|n|A variety of quartz, of a color between grass green and leek green, which is found associated with common chalcedony. It was much esteemed by the ancients for making engraved ornaments. ; The viscous material of an animal or vegetable cell, out of which the various tissues are formed by a process of differentiation; protoplasm. ; Unorganized material; elementary matter. ; A mixture of starch and glycerin, used as a substitute for ointments.	V:de6,89,2~de6,89,2	n:1gwg,133,3~1gwg,133,3	N:htm,144,9~htm,144,9
