1kqv|n|A plat; a plan; a sketch; a model; a pattern. Used also figuratively. ; A place laid out after a model. ; Any flat or horizontal surface; especially, one that is raised above some particular level, as a framework of timber or boards horizontally joined so as to form a roof, or a raised floor, or portion of a floor; a landing; a dais; a stage, for speakers, performers, or workmen; a standing place. ; A declaration of the principles upon which a person, a sect, or a party proposes to stand; a declared policy or system; as, the Saybrook platform; a political platform. ; A light deck, usually placed in a section of the hold or over the floor of the magazine. See Orlop.	a:9rd,73,166~9rd,73,166	v:1cbc,27,3;xx0,23,3;9rd,19,4;1n1q,1,4~1n1q,1,4;9rd,19,4;1cbc,27,3;xx0,23,3	V:w25,27,3;1cb9,24,2;1uhc,19,1~w25,27,3;1cb9,24,2;1uhc,19,1	n:1o50,41,6;9rg,33,2;1uno,17,5;9rd,9,2;1n1i,8,11;6wp,4,6~1n1i,8,11;6wp,4,6;1o50,41,6;1uno,17,5;9rd,9,2;9rg,33,2	N:1cb9,30,3;1wr5,26,4;1uhc,19,1;1cb5,15,1;138,10,1~1wr5,26,4;1cb9,30,3;1uhc,19,1;1cb5,15,1;138,10,1
